      "writtenOn": "2019-12-06T18:16:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue is not the precision of the variable but the atomicity of the operations on that variable. What I meant here is that 64-bit architectures operate on u64 using single instructions which prevents torn reads/writes. If we use this patch on 32-bit architecture then we should use atomic type to prevent torn values.",
      "parentUuid": "da845f5d_3fea6e64",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "d1d233dc15d6f543b3ea0b7a56a3850d0ea15c09",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "69a03796_e1a678a8",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/ion/ion_page_pool.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1275554
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-06T18:50:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the clarification.\n\nIf I understand your concern correctly, pool-\u003emutex will protect the race for updating part for nr_total_pages so only concern is reading part via ion_page_pool_nr_pages.\n\nI roughly remember if the variable is aligned to word boundary and size is word, it guarantees the atomicity. Not sure just declaring static variable like this guarantees word boundary align.\n(Just pass to other expert)\n\nThat means if you declare the variable as unsigned long, it could be word unit for each system unless I miss something. IOW, 32 bit in 32bit mahcine, 64bit in 64bit machine.\nSo if you declare the variable as \"unsgined long\" and you give the guarantee it\u0027s word size aligned, it doesn\u0027t have the load-store tearing problem in both systems, I think.",
      "parentUuid": "7c23df71_2dbf1658",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "d1d233dc15d6f543b3ea0b7a56a3850d0ea15c09",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2dc17e01_5cb390a5",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/ion/ion_page_pool.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-06T18:54:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "pool-\u003emutex is a pool-specific mutex while nr_total_pages is a counter for the total memory in all pools, so it would not be right to use it.\nLooks like we still have to support 32-bit kernels, so the cleanest way is to change it back to atomic_long_t similar to how vmstats are using atomics for their accounting.",
      "parentUuid": "69a03796_e1a678a8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "d1d233dc15d6f543b3ea0b7a56a3850d0ea15c09",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
