    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cb338ac0_3fc055d2",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/ion/ion_page_pool.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1275554
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-10T19:05:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hey Suren,\n\nI wanted to not make noise but I should agree with Greg so suggest the idea one more time.\n\nThing is ION heap allocation is one of hot path we have optimized to make faster or at least regression detection. It\u0027s rather hard to detect this kinds of tiny regression by atomic op so that someday, it would be huge once they are accumulated.\n\nAFAIK, if the variable is aligned and word-size, read/write could be atomic for both 32bit and 64bit.\nThat\u0027s why I suggested to declare unsigned long instead of u64 and guarantee it as \"aligned allocation\" by something if we need. Only remained concern is the value could be overflowed because it doesn\u0027t have barrier if the race happens(but it could be okay for atomic point of view) so what we need further is just\n\nlong get_something(void) {\n  if (val \u003c 0)\n    val \u003d 0;\n  return val;\n}\n\nIf the race is very tiny, it doesn\u0027t make big difference in real practice.",
      "parentUuid": "87371412_d0ee1bc8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 70
      },
